<title>CROATIA: Austrian firm buys stake in Croatian gypsum plant.</title>
<headline>Austrian firm buys stake in Croatian gypsum plant.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian firm Knauf GmbH bought a 42.27 percent stake in Croatian gypsum plant Kningips at a state privatisation agency auction on Thursday, the Zagreb Stock Exchange reported.</p>
<p>It said in a press release a total of 21,437 shares were sold for 3.54 million German marks or 12.6 million kuna to the only bidder via a local broker I.F.C.</p>
<p>The price was said to be 50 percent higher than the value Kningips shares were issued at.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
